WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
The agent writes tests. The worker reruns them and checks they fail when

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:18.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
the app filter is deliberately broken.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:27.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Only synthetic app source is provided to the model. No production site,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:36.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
credentials or customer browser session is involved.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:46.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
The downloadable example supplies the fixture, complete prompt, worker,

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:56.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
artifact checks and cleanup. No paid model fallback.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:05.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Expected results come from the caller. The agent receives an app and

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:14.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
requirements, not a prewritten test suite.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:25.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
These commands run inside the sandbox, not on your worker. Do not assume

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:36.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
stock OpenCode includes a browser.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:46.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
The local health check must succeed. Detached returns a job handle, not

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:56.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
a ready application.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:08.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
The agent must observe real rows, select Passed, restore All and capture

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:20.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
the result in Chromium.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:32.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
The prompt names every output and forbids fabricated results. The worker

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:44.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
still independently checks acceptance.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:55.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
The four-minute agent command runs in /workspace. Raw reasoning stays

00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:06.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
private; only reviewed evidence is published.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:16.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
The recorded assertion reads browser state. The later mutation check

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:26.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
proves it rejects the extra visible rows.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:36.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Fresh artifacts must be created. Existing output from the agent run

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:46.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
cannot satisfy the independent rerun.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:55.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
A real 1280 x 720 Chromium screenshot, downloaded through the Harakiri

00:03:55.000 --> 00:04:04.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
SDK after the independent run.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:13.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Real 390 x 844 screenshot. The generated test reports no horizontal

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:22.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
overflow for this fixture.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:34.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
A browser startup error is not accepted as regression detection. The

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:46.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
broken filter must trigger an assertion failure.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:56.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
Original app passes. Broken filter fails. Screenshots downloaded. Model

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:06.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
steps reported zero cost in this run.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:16.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
The capture independently confirms termination. Setup failures,

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:26.000 line:92% position:50% size:90% align:center
unavailable models and failed assertions also require cleanup.
